# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# There is deliberately NO `/* /index.html 200` catch-all any more. Every route
# in ROUTES (src/site.config.ts) is prerendered to its own dist/<path>/index.html
# by the `portfolio-seo` plugin, so Pages serves those as real static files. A
# blanket SPA fallback would also answer genuinely unknown URLs with HTTP 200 —
# a "soft 404" that search engines index as a real page. Without it, anything
# unmatched falls through to dist/404.html with a proper 404 status, and the
# client router still renders the NotFound route inside that shell.
#
# The exception is /learnings/*: those routes exist in the client router
# (App.tsx) but aren't in ROUTES, so no static file is emitted for them and they
# still need the SPA shell. @sync: add a rule here for any future client route
# that isn't added to ROUTES.
/learnings      /index.html   200
/learnings/*    /index.html   200
